# PERMIT DENIED — project contract

One compact demolition arcade. Same town every run. No meta, no campaign, no second map.

**Title** on the page: `PERMIT DENIED`. Tagline: “The County Said No.”

## Doc authority

- `README.md` is how to run, controls, current scope, and where the game is hosted.

## Stack lock

TypeScript + Vite + PixiJS v8. Entirely client-side. Simulation in world coordinates; isometric projection is render-only. Fixed timestep. No React on the game canvas. No backend, accounts, or API keys.

## Stay on the lot

Keep out of this build: title/campaign/meta, JSON schemas, plugin systems, between-run unlocks, a second town, ECS, React wrappers around the canvas.

Buildings are per-cell destructible with a support/collapse model. Visual debris is garnish; rubble collides and matches the wreck.

Copy: `BLADE UP` / `BLADE DOWN`, deaths `ENGINE COOKED` / `TRACK THROWN` / `COUNTY CLOCK`. Do not write Heemeyer, Granby, manifesto, or wanted stars.

## Done

Playable three-minute demolition run with driving, localized damage, cascading collapse, rubble, HUD, upgrades, and audio.
